# Verifies builtin-cap-env-has? returns Int(1) when a cap IS present in scope.
# Creates a child scope of root (scope 0) injecting %cwd from the environment.
# The %cwd thunk carries span.name="%cwd" (set by the CLI injection), so the scope
# lookup finds it by name. Tests the Rust-level Int(1) protocol for the present case.
[call [fn [let]
  [child-scope: [builtin-scope-new 0 [%cwd: %cwd]]]
  [result: [builtin-cap-env-has? "%cwd" child-scope]]
  result]]
=== out
Int(1)
